       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the maximum prescription dose for adults (3,200 mg/day), and the usual maximum for a single dose is 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common dose for mild to moderate pain\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), which is typical for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum, which is generally used short-term\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into a different schedule\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give me a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still advise against it."
      }
